# OpenTDF TDF3 for Swift

Experimental SwiftPM library product/module `OpenTDFTDF3`, built from shared Go
source with Goalchemy. Requires Swift 6.4.0, a C compiler, pkg-config, OpenSSL 3,
zlib and libcurl development packages. Linux x86_64 is the verified baseline;
macOS and iOS integration have not been verified.

Add this directory as a SwiftPM dependency and depend on its `OpenTDFTDF3`
product. `encrypt(config, Data(...), options).wait()` returns encrypted `Data`;
`decrypt(config, archive).wait()` returns owned payload, metadata and manifest
bytes. Use `.value()` with `await` for asynchronous callers. Operations are lazy,
serialized, and accept cancellation, deadlines and typed token providers.

Configuration fields retain their Go names. Text uses `GoString`; literals are
UTF-8, and `GoString(bytes: ...)` preserves arbitrary bytes. Slice fields are
optional arrays so nil and empty remain distinct. Failures throw `TDFError`
with code, operation, HTTP status, server fields and cancellation category.
No Go runtime is invoked. Goalchemy's runtime license is included in `LICENSE`.
